Fixed several bugs in the M340 SNMP pull: the communication services flags were reversed, Port 502 and web server status always read as "no configuration", the MAC address was garbled, ``system_uptime`` was read from ``ifTableLastChange`` instead of ``sysUpTime``, and a missing slot or fewer than 5 LEDs raised an exception. The M340 pull now also uses the SNMP community that worked during verification and the ``snmp`` port and timeout options. In ``peat.protocols.snmp``, table indices with IP addresses are no longer garbled, ``sysObjectID`` and other OID values are no longer dropped, and walks keep their partial results after a timeout and no longer return empty or duplicated final entries.
